        <UserObject label="" tooltip="Execution and evidence contracts&#10;&#10;In the app: `?node=exec-header`&#10;&#10;Text outline of execution-contracts.svg; the primary accessible reading form of that diagram. Each anchor equals the node id in `pipeline-model.json`, the `&lt;g id&gt;` in the SVG and the object id in the `.drawio` file, whose single link per object points back to this anchor. &quot;In the app&quot; gives each node's location in the workbench, which resolves it against the active project. Symbols that carry meaning are spelled out in words.&#10;&#10;Summary: Reading order: three task steps (declare, admit, compute outside the commit), three independent binding proofs (bytes, identity, operation), independent acceptance feeding separate original-code and recovered-source capabilities, then fence, quarantine and continue, and the late-worker design challenge. Missing evidence blocks only its own claim, an unhealthy resource blocks its dependents, and ready independent work continues. Design specification only: the late-worker experiment and all future software acceptance checks are NOT RUN; execution-contracts.outline.md is the text outline.&#10;&#10;Design specification, companion to the recovery overview, future software acceptance checks NOT RUN&#10;&#10;Missing evidence blocks its claim. An unhealthy resource blocks its dependents. Ready independent work continues." link="execution-contracts.outline.md#exec-header" id="exec-header"><mxCell style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="9.4" width="1145.04" height="103.9" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject>
